  "question": {
    "text": "In alkaline medium, the reduction of permanganate anion involves a gain of ____________ electrons.&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In Faintly alkaline medium potassium permanganate changes to manganese dioxide in its oxidising action.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>The oxidation state of manganese in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;is +7 and in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is +4.</p><p>Hence, it transfers 3 electrons during the oxidising action in alkaline medium.</p>"
  }
}